Two decisions worth noting:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- I call libc [38;5;10mprintf[0m through an [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m declaration rather than Rust's [38;5;10mprintln![0m. Since this is a [38;5;10mcdylib[0m linked into C programs, going through the same [38;5;10mstdout[0m [38;5;10mFILE[0m stream preserves buffering and interleaving with the caller's own output — Rust's independently-buffered stdout could reorder lines.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m2*x[0m overflows for [38;5;10m|x| > 2^30[0m, which is UB in C but wraps in the emitted code. I used [38;5;10mwrapping_mul[0m/[38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m to reproduce that instead of panicking in debug builds.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I checked the header for namespace-renaming macros; there are none, so the linker symbol is plain [38;5;10mdriver[0m, confirmed via [38;5;10mnm[0m ([38;5;10mT driver[0m).[0m[0m
